// After every dpkg run, check that each kernel in /boot has an NVIDIA module
// matching the userspace driver, and send an ntfy alert if one does not.
//
// Why: the prebuilt module is a separate package per kernel, so any path that
// installs a kernel without it leaves one that boots with the panel on the
// firmware framebuffer. That stays invisible until the reboot, which can be
// days later; this reports it in the run that caused it.
//
// Scope: detection only. It never fails the transaction, because the fix is
// itself an apt run that has to be able to proceed. The alert names the host.
//
// Revert: rm this file, /usr/local/sbin/nvidia-module-check and
// /usr/local/sbin/ntfy
DPkg::Post-Invoke {
    "if [ -x /usr/local/sbin/nvidia-module-check ]; then /usr/local/sbin/nvidia-module-check --alert || true; fi";
};
